on node2, both using shared identity dataops (UID/GID 4500) and directory ownership dataops:dataops mode 2770. Verified cross-node file consistency, then performed the mandatory sequential restart of node1 and node2 with proof of changed boot identity and full post-restart recovery of NFS export/mount and data.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Created dataops user/group (UID/GID 4500) identically on node1 and node2\",\"Installed nfs-kernel-server on node1 and nfs-common on node2\",\"Created /srv/nfs/shared on node1, chown dataops:dataops, chmod 2770\",\"Configured /etc/exports restricting export to node2's IP with root_squash, enabled+started nfs-kernel-server, ran exportfs -ra\",\"Created /mnt/shared on node2, added fstab entry with _netdev, mounted the NFSv4 share\",\"Verified cross-node file creation as dataops preserves dataops:dataops ownership and mode 2770 on both nodes\",\"Verified root is denied write access due to root_squash + mode 2770 (expected security behavior)\",\"Captured baseline boot_id and health on node1 and node2\",\"Restarted node1 via systemctl reboot (backgrounded), polled until reachable, confirmed new boot_id, confirmed nfs-kernel-server active, export present, and shared directory data/ownership intact\",\"Confirmed node2's hard NFS mount survived node1's restart without manual remount and wrote a new file successfully\",\"Restarted node2 via systemctl reboot (backgrounded), polled until reachable, confirmed new boot_id, confirmed /mnt/shared auto-mounted via fstab, all prior files present with correct ownership, and successfully wrote a new file\",\"Final consistency check on node1 confirming all files from both nodes visible with correct ownership after both restarts\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"dataops user/group UID/GID 4500 created identically on both nodes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e855fd04b74a441b\",\"cmd-294cf4aae5444bf6\"],\"summary\":\"id dataops on node1 and node2 both show uid=4500(dataops) gid=4500(dataops)\"},{\"requirement\