ter boot, shared directory data/ownership intact; node2's hard mount continued working without remount\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4913807d351244cb\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id 4d70780a-0bff-4d50-8c53-62faa1ccc945 captured, mount active and healthy\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1fc05597f21442f4\",\"cmd-6657159fa797420b\",\"cmd-3b9780be85224da7\"],\"summary\":\"reboot command acknowledged before disconnect, node2 unreachable during reboot, new boot_id b7005841-9481-47eb-aa65-beb07671bf4f confirms restart occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 post-restart recovery of NFS mount and data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1478384dcae74694\",\"cmd-7f50d342abf441eb\"],\"summary\":\"mount auto-recovered via fstab _netdev entry on boot, all prior files visible with correct dataops:dataops ownership, new file write succeeded and is visible from node1 too\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured NFS export of /srv/nfs/shared on node1 and mounted it at /mnt/shared on node2, both using shared identity dataops (UID/GID 4500) and directory ownership dataops:dataops mode 2770. Verified cross-node file consistency, then performed the mandatory sequential restart of node1 and node2 with proof of changed boot identity and full post-restart recovery of NFS export/mount and data.","actions_performed":["Created dataops user/group (UID/GID 4500) identically on node1 and node2","Installed nfs-kernel-server on node1 and nfs-common on node2","Created /srv/nfs/shared on node1, chown dataops:dataops, chmod 2770","Configured /etc/exports restricting export to node2's IP with root_squash, enabled+started nfs-kernel-server, ran exportfs -ra","Created /mnt/shared on node2, added fstab entry with _netdev, mounted the NFSv4 share","Verified cross-node file creation as dataops preserves dataops:dataops ownership and mode 2770 on both nodes","Verified root is